-- title:
--   Kerr in ingoing (Kerr's original) coordinates: metric, candidate inverse, domain
-- statement:
--   In coordinates $(v,r,\theta,\varphi)=(x_0,x_1,x_2,x_3)$, $\Sigma=r^2+a^2\cos^2\theta$, $F=1-2Mr/\Sigma$, $A=a\sin^2\theta$, the **ingoing Kerr metric** $g^{\rm in}_{M,a}$ has $g_{vv}=-F$, $g_{vr}=g_{rv}=1$, $g_{v\varphi}=g_{\varphi v}=(1-F)A$, $g_{r\varphi}=g_{\varphi r}=A$, $g_{\theta\theta}=\Sigma$, $g_{\varphi\varphi}=(2-F)A^2+\Sigma\sin^2\theta$ and all other entries $0$; this is Visser's line element $ds^2=-F(dv+A\,d\varphi)^2+2(dv+A\,d\varphi)(dr+A\,d\varphi)+\Sigma(d\theta^2+\sin^2\theta\,d\varphi^2)$ read with the half-Hessian convention ($g_{vr}=1$ from $2\,dv\,dr$). The **candidate inverse** $\hat g^{\rm in}_{M,a}$ has $\hat g^{vv}=a^2\sin^2\theta/\Sigma$, $\hat g^{vr}=\hat g^{rv}=(r^2+a^2)/\Sigma$, $\hat g^{v\varphi}=\hat g^{\varphi v}=\hat g^{r\varphi}=\hat g^{\varphi r}=-a/\Sigma$, $\hat g^{rr}=(r^2-2Mr+a^2)/\Sigma$, $\hat g^{\theta\theta}=1/\Sigma$, $\hat g^{\varphi\varphi}=1/(\Sigma\sin^2\theta)$, other entries $0$. The **domain** is $U^{\rm in}_a=\{x:\ \Sigma\neq0,\ \sin\theta\neq0\}$ (there is no $\Delta\neq0$ restriction; a point with $\Delta=0$ lies in the domain precisely when it also satisfies $\Sigma\neq0$ and $\sin\theta\neq0$). Also the equatorial point $(0,\rho,\pi/2,0)$.
--
--   **Clarification of the preserved source comment (2026-10-14).** The published Lean text of this bundle keeps its original module docstring. The comment does not affect the Lean definitions and is left unchanged (published payloads are immutable; no replacement node was created). Three phrases there are to be read as follows. (i) “Visser's `u` is called `v` here (it is the advanced null coordinate)”: $v$ is an advanced-type coordinate; the radial coordinate vector $\partial_r$ is null ($g_{rr}=0$), but for $a\neq0$ the covector $dv$ is not null, since $\hat g^{vv}=a^2\sin^2\theta/\Sigma\neq0$ on the domain (where $\hat g$ is the inverse by `ExactVacuumAtlas.Kerr.In.cert`); no claim is made that the hypersurfaces $v=\text{const}$ are null. (ii) “…, all other entries `0`” after a list naming only $g_{vr}$, $g_{v\varphi}$, $g_{r\varphi}$ among the off-diagonal entries: the matrix is symmetric, and the definition `gIn` sets $g_{rv}$, $g_{\varphi v}$, $g_{\varphi r}$ to the same values; only the remaining entries are $0$. (iii) “the coordinate locus `Δ = 0` (horizon radii, as a name only) lies inside the domain”: there is no $\Delta\neq0$ restriction, and a point with $\Delta=0$ lies in the domain precisely when it also satisfies $\Sigma\neq0$ and $\sin\theta\neq0$; whether such points exist depends on $(M,a)$ (`ExactVacuumAtlas.Release01.coverage` gives one for $M>0$, $a^2\le M^2$).
